 are plotted from figures provided by the Office of Market Finance. See Table FD-5.)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 351, 1430, 1890], \"page_id\": 39}], \"content\": null, \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"figure\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 116, 171, 141], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"38\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [452, 203, 1175, 243], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Public Debt Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 290, 794, 592], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Chapter 31 of Title 31 of the United States Code allows the Secretary of Treasury to borrow money by issuing Treasury securities. The Secretary determines the terms and conditions of issue, conversion, maturity, payment and interest rate. New issues of Treasury notes mature in 2 to 10 years. Bonds mature in more than 10 years from the issue date. Each outstanding marketable security is listed in the \\u201cMonthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States.\\u201d The information in this section of the \\u201cTreasury Bulletin\\u201d pertains only to marketable Treasury securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 596, 792, 806], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-1 provides a maturity schedule of interest-bearing marketable Treasury notes and bonds. All unmatured Treasury notes and bonds are listed in maturity order, from earliest to latest. A separate breakout is provided for the combined holdings of the Government accounts and Federal Reserve Banks (FRBs), so that the \\u201call other investors\\u201d category includes all private holdings.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 297, 1488, 504], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-2 presents the results of weekly auctions of 4-, 13- and 26-week bills. Treasury bills mature each Thursday. Issues of 4- and 13-week bills are reopenings of 26-week bills. Issues of cash management bills also are presented. High yields on accepted tenders and the dollar value of total bids are presented, with the dollar value of awards made on both competitive and noncompetitive bases.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 507, 1488, 622], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"To encourage the participation of individuals and smaller institutions, Treasury accepts noncompetitive tenders of up to $1 million for bills and $5 million for notes and bonds in each auction of securities.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 629, 1488, 719], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-3 lists the results of auctions of marketable securities, other than weekly bills, in chronological order over the past 2 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 726, 1488, 870], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Table PDO-4 indicates the total amount of marketable securities allotted to each class of investor. The FRBs tally into investor classes the tenders in each auction of marketable securities other than weekly auctions of 4-, 13- and 26-week bills.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [421, 896, 1204, 929], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: JULY-SEPTEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [510, 955, 1122, 985], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"[Source: Bureau of the Public Debt, Office of Financing]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1016, 794, 1202], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On July 23, 2001, Treasury announced plans to begin regular weekly offerings of 4-week bills. The first 4-week bill was announced July 30, auctioned July 31 and issued August 2.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 1268, 224, 1299], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"JULY\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1322, 665, 1346], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Auction of 9-1/2-Year Inflation-Indexed Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1360, 792, 1443], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On July 5, 2001, Treasury announced it would auction $5,000 million of 9-1/2 year inflation-indexed notes to raise cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1450, 794, 1617], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"The 9-1/2-year 3-1/2 percent inflation-indexed notes of Series A-2011 were dated January 15, 2001, and issued July 16, 2001. They are due January 15, 2011, with interest payable on January 15 and July 15 until maturity. Accrued interest of $0.09511 per $1,000 covering the period from July 15, to July 16, 2001, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1624, 794, 1902], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon eastern daylight saving time (e.d.s.t.) for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.s.t. for competitive tenders on July 11. Tenders totaled $9,505 million; Treasury accepted $5,000 million at the high yield of 3.500 percent with an equivalent adjusted price of 101.863. Treasury accepted in full, all competitive tenders at yields lower than 3.500 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 86.09 percent. The median yield was 3.468 percent, and the low yield was 3.430 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $111 million. Competitive\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1009, 1490, 1096], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"tenders accepted from private investors totaled $4,889 million. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of inflation-indexed notes is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1110, 1115, 1136], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1150, 1490, 1259], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"On July 18, Treasury announced it would auction $12,000 million of 2-year notes of Series S-2003. The issue was to re-fund $28,510 million of securities maturing July 31 and to pay down about $16.510 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1268, 1490, 1410], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series S-2003 were dated and issued July 31, 2001. They are due July 31, 2003, with interest payable on January 31 and July 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 3-7/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1414, 1490, 1718], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.d.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.s.t. for competitive tenders on July 25. Tenders totaled $29,506 million; Treasury accepted $12,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 3.965 percent with the equivalent price of $99.829. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 45.37 percent. The median yield was 3.940 percent, and the low yield was 3.900 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $1,085 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,915 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1728, 1490, 1810], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $12,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $4,000 million from Federal Reserve Banks (FRBs) for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1817, 1490, 1872], \"page_id\": 40}], \"content\": \"The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series S-2003 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [636, 116, 994, 141], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1454, 113, 1490, 139], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"39\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [384, 203, 1246, 240], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: JULY-SEPTEMBER, con\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 278, 415, 304], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Cash Management Bills\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 316, 794, 488], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On June 28, 2001, Treasury announced that it would auction $13,000 million of 9-day bills to be issued July 3, 2001, and to mature July 12, 2001. The issue was to raise new cash. Treasury auctioned the bills on July 2, 2001. Tenders totaled $40,000 million; Treasury accepted $13,000 million. The high bank discount rate was 3.75 percent.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 507, 443, 533], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Debt Buyback Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 547, 794, 660], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on July 19, 2001, for settlement on July 23, Treasury received $6,079 million of offers. It accepted $1,500 million par amount for a total price paid of $1,746 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 667, 794, 778], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on July 26, 2001, for settlement on July 30, Treasury received $6,078 million of offers. It accepted $1,000 million par amount for a total price paid of $1,384 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 816, 282, 844], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"AUGUST\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [144, 874, 470, 900], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"August Quarterly Financing\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 917, 794, 1082], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On August 1, Treasury announced it would auction $11,000 million of 4-3/4-year notes of Series E-2006; $11,000 million of 10-year notes of Series C-2011; and $5,000 million of 29-1/2-year bonds of February 2031. The issue was to refund $11,885 million of Treasury securities maturing August 15 and to raise about $15,115 million of new cash.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1089, 794, 1256], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"The 4-3/4-year 4-5/8 percent notes of Series E-2006 were dated May 15, 2001 and issued August 15, 2001. They are due May 15, 2006, with interest payable on November 15 and May 15 until maturity. Accrued interest of $11.56250 per $1,000, covering the period from May 15 to August 15, 2001, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1263, 794, 1598], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.d.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.s.t. for competitive tenders on August 7. Tenders totaled $23,626 million; Treasury accepted $11,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 4.670 percent with an equivalent price of 99.797. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 4.670 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 95.66 percent. The median yield was 4.651 percent, and the low yield was 4.600 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $178 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,822 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1605, 794, 1716], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $11,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $623 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of Series E-2006 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1723, 794, 1864], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"The 10-year notes of Series C-2011 were dated and issued August 15, 2001. They are due August 15, 2011, with interest payable on February 15 and August 15 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 5 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 14, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [142, 1874, 794, 1926], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.d.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.s.t. for\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 15, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 276, 1490, 549], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"competitive tenders on August 8. Tenders totaled $31,352 million; Treasury accepted $11,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 5.078 percent with an equivalent price of 99.394. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 5.078. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 63.72 percent. The median yield was 5.070 percent, and the low yield was 5.030 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $108 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $10,892 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 16, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 561, 1490, 672], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $11,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $1,043 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series C-2011 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 17, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 681, 1490, 794], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"The 29-1/2-year 5-3/8 percent bonds of February 2031 were dated February 15, 2001 and issued August 15, 2001. They are due February 15, 2031, with interest payable on February 15 and August 15 until maturity.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 18, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 804, 1490, 1136], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the bonds before 12 noon e.d.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.s.t. for competitive tenders on August 9. Tenders totaled $10,805 million; Treasury accepted $5,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 5.520 percent with an equivalent price of 97.900. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 5.520 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 7.10 percent. The median yield was 5.472 percent, and the low yield was 5.400 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $32 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $4,968 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 19, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1146, 1490, 1256], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $5,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $540 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of bonds of February 2031 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 20, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1278, 1115, 1301], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 21, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1325, 1490, 1433], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"On August 22, the Treasury announced that it would auction $14,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $28,397 million of securities maturing August 31 and to pay down about $14,397 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 22, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1445, 1490, 1584], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series T-2003 were dated and issued August 31, 2001. They are due August 31, 2003, with interest payable on February 28 and August 31 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 3-5/8 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 23, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 1591, 1490, 1926], \"page_id\": 41}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.d.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.d.s.t. for competitive tenders on August 29. Tenders totaled $30,314 million; Treasury accepted $14,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 3.685 percent with an equivalent price of 99.885. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 31.45 percent. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 3.685 percent. The median yield was 3.650 percent, and the low yield was 3.620 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $1,095 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $12,905 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 24, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 111, 188, 146], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"40\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [632, 113, 1005, 144], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [379, 203, 1260, 248], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"TREASURY FINANCING: JULY-SEPTEMBER, con.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [126, 283, 805, 380], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $14,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $4,667 million from FRBs for their own accounts.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 396, 448, 431], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Debt Buyback Operations\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 455, 803, 578], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on August 16, 2001, for settlement on August 20, Treasury received $10,451 million of offers. It accepted $1,750 million par amount for a total price paid of $2,475 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [131, 580, 803, 702], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"In the debt buyback operation held on August 23, 2001, for settlement on August 27, Treasury received $6,764 million of offers. It accepted $1,750 million par amount for a total price paid of $2,364 million (less accrued interest).\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 733, 355, 771], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"SEPTEMBER\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 804, 428, 839], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Auction of 2-Year Notes\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [129, 863, 803, 983], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"On September 19, Treasury announced it would auction $17,000 million of 2-year notes. The issue was to refund $27,178 million of securities maturing September 30 and to pay down about $10,178 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [831, 283, 1504, 523], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"The notes of Series U-2003 were dated September 30, 2001 and issued October 1, 2001. They are due September 30, 2003, with interest payable on March 31 and September 30 until maturity. Treasury set an interest rate of 2-3/4 percent after determining which tenders were accepted on a yield auction basis. Accrued interest of $0.07555 per $1,000, covering the period from September 30, to October 1, 2001, was payable with each accepted tender.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [838, 526, 1506, 860], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"Treasury received tenders for the notes before 12 noon e.d.s.t. for noncompetitive tenders and before 1 p.m. e.s.t. for competitive tenders on September 26. Tenders totaled $41,181 million; Treasury accepted $17,000 million. All noncompetitive and successful competitive bidders were allotted securities at the high yield of 2.869 percent with an equivalent price of 99.770. Treasury accepted in full all competitive tenders at yields lower than 2.869 percent. Tenders at the high yield were allotted 49.03 percent. The median yield was 2.820 percent, and the low yield was 2.790 percent. Noncompetitive tenders totaled $919 million. Competitive tenders accepted from private investors totaled $16,081 million.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [840, 865, 1506, 988], \"page_id\": 42}], \"content\": \"In addition to the $17,000 million of tenders accepted in the auction process, Treasury accepted $5,667 million from FRBs for their own accounts. The minimum par amount required for STRIPS of notes of Series U-2003 is $1,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [634, 101, 996, 125], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"PUBLIC DEBT OPERATIONS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1454, 97, 1484, 125], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"41\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [189, 196, 1435, 264], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"TABLE PDO-1.\\u2014Maturity Schedules of Interest-Bearing Marketable Public Debt Securities Other than Regular Weekly and 52-Week Treasury Bills Outstanding, Sept. 30, 2001\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [166, 290, 1459, 316], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"[In millions of dollars. Sources: \\u201cMonthly Statement of the Public Debt of the United States;\\u201d Bureau of the Public Debt, Office of Public Debt Accounting; and Office of Market Finance]\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [146, 337, 1484, 1862], \"page_id\": 43}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Date of final maturity</th><th>Description (1)</th><th>Issue date (2)</th><th>Total (3)</th><th>U.S. Government and Federal Reserve Banks (4)</th><th>All other investors (5)</th></tr><tr><td>2001</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Oct. 31</td><td>6-1/4%-P note</td><td>10/31/96</td><td>14,640</td><td>2,433</td><td>12,207</td></tr><tr><td>Oct. 31</td><td>1 5-7/8%-AE note</td><td>11/01/99</td><td>19,196</td><td>3,710</td><td>15,486</td></tr><tr><td>Nov. 15</td><td>15-3/4% bond</td><td>10/07/81</td><td>1,753</td><td>291</td